  "problem": [
   {
    "lang": "en",
    "value": "Palo Alto Networks is aware of two critical vulnerabilities in PHP: CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619.\n\nCVE-2026-109618 involves a remote code execution vulnerability where handling out-of-memory errors via longjmp() leaves request memory uninitialized due to improper control flow management, allowing attackers to reliably achieve RCE using out-of-memory (OOM) triggers.\n\nCVE-2026-109619 describe"
   }
  ],
  "solution": [
   {
    "lang": "eng",
    "value": "PAN-OS\n\nThis issue will be fixed in the upcoming releases of PAN-OS. This advisory will be updated with fixed versions and release estimates as they become available.\n\n\n\nUntil PAN-OS fix versions are available we recommend implementing the workaround and mitigations listed below.\n\nSee https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/cve-2026-109618-cve-2026-109619/ for more details on the Palo Alto Networks pr"
   }
  ],
  "work_around": [
   {
    "lang": "eng",
    "value": "Customers with Frontier Virtual Patching (https://www.paloaltonetworks.com/blog/network-security/harnessing-ai-for-prevention-introducing-frontier-virtual-patching/) (ATP Plus) on PAN-OS 12.2.4 and later versions received advance coverage, released via Threat ID 543004, which was released at 10:21 PM PT on Oct 20.\n\n\nCustomers with a Threat Prevention subscription are provided with coverage against"
   }
  ],
