  "problem": [
   {
    "lang": "en",
    "value": "A remote code execution (RCE) vulnerability in the management interface of Palo Alto Networks PAN-OS\u00ae software enables an authenticated attacker with network access to execute arbitrary code with root privileges on the firewall.\n\nThe security risk posed by this issue is minimized by restricting access to the management interface to only trusted internal IP addresses according to our recommended\u00a0be"
   }
  ],
  "solution": [
   {
    "lang": "eng",
    "value": "VERSION           MINOR VERSION                SUGGESTED SOLUTION\nCloud NGFW                                     No action needed.\nPAN-OS 12.2       12.2.0 through 12.2.3        Upgrade to 12.2.4 or later.\nPAN-OS 12.1       12.1.8 through 12.1.10-h*    Upgrade to 12.1.10-h2 or later.\n                  12.1.5 through 12.1.7-h*     Upgrade to 12.1.7-h8 or 12.1.10-h2 or later.\n                  12.1."
   }
  ],
  "work_around": [
   {
    "lang": "eng",
    "value": "No known workarounds exist for this issue.\n\nCustomers with a Threat Prevention subscription are provided with limited coverage against this vulnerability by enabling Threat ID\u00a0510046 and 510047 (from Applications and Threats content version 9159-10287 and later). For these Threat IDs to protect against attacks for this vulnerability:\n\n\n\n * Route incoming traffic for the MGT port through a DP port "
   }
  ],
